       "Chronicler",
       "Three years after the great battle, King Jogaila and Grand Duke Vytautas came to Samogitia themselves. Długosz writes that they cut down the groves and put out the fires. Great-grandfather did not tell it so. He said that it was cold, and that the king spoke to the people in our tongue."
